<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 3-mth T-bills 98 pct sold, yielding 69 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 3-mth T-bills 98 pct sold, yielding 69 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of nine billion levs of three-month floater coupon T-bills was 97.72 percent sold, yielding 69.39 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 15 percent monthly or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		    BG 3020196021</p>
<p> Par value			 9.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date		    November 4, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			November 6, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		   February 5, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		   8,999.9 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	     85.31 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		   8,794.5 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	    85.53 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity   69.39 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
